WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
We are now moving into a section that can be emotionally difficult to discuss,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:11.440
child CPR. According to AHA guidelines, a child is defined as someone between the

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.760
ages of one and puberty. While it is heavy to think about,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.480
remember that your training is what gives a child

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.680
the best chance in an emergency. Most cardiac arrests in children and

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:29.360
infants are not caused by heart problems like they are in adults. Instead, they are

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.599
usually respiratory in nature, meaning they stem from a breathing

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.880
emergency like choking, drowning, seizures, or

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.639
suffocation. Regardless of the cause, once the heart

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:44.160
stops, the life-saving steps remain very similar

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.880
to what we have already learned. Here are the adjusted steps for CPR on a

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.240
child between the ages of one and eight. One, ensure your scene is safe before

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.080
you approach. Two, assess the child by tapping their

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.200
shoulders and shouting to check for responsiveness.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.120
Look for severe signs like a lack of consciousness or blue lips and

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.760
extremities. Three, call for help. Point to someone to

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.959
call 9-1-1 and get an AED.

00:01:12.959 --> 00:01:16.800
If you are alone, put your phone on speakerphone and start CPR

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.160
immediately. If you don't have a phone and are alone,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.400
perform five rounds of CPR first, then go find help.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.919
Four, start CPR beginning with compressions.

00:01:27.919 --> 00:01:32.320
Because children are smaller, you can use one or two arms depending on what is

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.320
needed to reach the ideal depth. Take a moment to look at the images on

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.919
the screen showing the one-handed and two-handed techniques.

00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:43.839
Maintain your rhythm of 100 to 120 beats per minute.

00:01:43.839 --> 00:01:47.440
After 30 compressions, open the airway with a head tilt

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.440
and chin lift. Pinch the nose, seal your mouth over theirs,

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.199
and give two breaths looking for that clear chest rise.

00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:59.120
Continue your 30 to 2 ratio until EMS arrives

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.080
or the child shows obvious signs of life. Now please pair up with your partner at

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.879
your mannequins. We are going to practice these

00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:10.080
adjustments together.

